+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+// Runtime hook events + fight tracker (phase 3, run #23: the 17 HOOK
+// achievements; #46 stays pending — see the notes in the registry
+// and in EvaluateBossDefeat / hook-run23-progress.md).
+//
+// Two kinds of runtime signal, one latch:
+//   * Direct calls from actor code (Heishi2 bribe #35, cow milk #38,
+//     Hyrule Loach #90) via Achievements_NotifyHook().
+//   * GameInteractor hooks registered here: OnActorInit arms the fight
+//     tracker when a boss spawns, OnBossDefeat evaluates the fight, and
+//     OnActorInit for the attack cucco fires #44 (Cuccos' Revenge).
+// Every signal only latches sHookFired[id]; Tick() turns it into the
+// normal unlock + toast on its own path (CheckCondition reads the latch
+// first), so all unlock logic stays in one place and nothing here writes
+// a CVar or a toast from inside an actor update.
+//
+// Fight tracker design (verified against the real 9.3.0 code):
+//   * Arming: OnActorInit of the boss actor, once per spawn. Re-entering
+//     a boss room after a death re-arms (fresh flags), so a failed attempt
+//     never poisons the next one.
+//   * Baselines: snapshotted on the first frame the player is out of the
+//     intro cutscene. This skips Zelda's full heal before Ganondorf
+//     (z_boss_ganon.c) and any intro-only state; damage/heals before the
+//     baselines do not exist (actors are halted during the cutscene).
+//   * Polling: every frame (Tick()'s unthrottled part, 20 Hz logic —
+//     GameState_Update / game.c:357, R_UPDATE_RATE = 3). Health is polled,
+//     not hooked: OnPlayerHealthChange misses bottle heals (the
+//     healthAccumulator drains +4/frame straight into gSaveContext.health
+//     with no hook, z_parameter.c), so any health increase = a heal and
+//     any decrease = damage. Fairies and bombs are polled by count/ammo
+//     (a used fairy leaves its bottle; ammo only decreases by use).
+//   * Verdict: in the OnBossDefeat hook, which fires on the killing blow,
+//     before the death cutscene and before any post-fight healing. The
+//     tracker is disarmed right after the verdict.
+//   * Timer (#93, Barinade < 1:51 with 3 hearts): frames counted from the
+//     baselines to the defeat, 20 ticks/s, so 111 s = 2220 ticks. Frame
+//     counting (not GAMEPLAYSTAT_TOTAL_TIME) because the time macro freezes
+//     at the Ganon defeat timestamp once the game is complete, which would
+//     false-positive #93 on any later Barinade replay / Boss Rush.
+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+static bool sHookFired[1024] = {};
+
+extern "C" void Achievements_NotifyHook(int achievementId) {
+    if (achievementId > 0 && achievementId < 1024) {
+        sHookFired[achievementId] = true;
+    }
+}
